When you add the std.lv <http://std.lv>=T argument, you have to take out the parts of the model syntax that are involved in this constraint. As the syntax will come first and still affect the model

The warning about the target from stan is a "false" warning. From how the model is defined, but actually doesnt cause any problem

If you can share th output from stanclassic/stancond, to see how "bad" is the convergence for these models?

